---
// src/components/About.astro

// 无需额外导入其他组件，这里只是单纯的一个展示区块
---

<section
  class="relative bg-background w-full max-w-screen-2xl flex justify-center items-center px-4 py-20 sm:py-24"
>
  <div
    class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-10 w-full max-w-2xl justify-center items-center"
  >
    <!-- 左侧：图片容器 -->
    <div
      class="flex-shrink-0 w-full max-w-[200px] h-[300px] bg-accent rounded-lg overflow-hidden perfect-shadow"
    >
      <img
        src="/assets/aac-7.png"
        alt="AAC For All Illustration"
        loading="lazy"
        class="w-full h-full object-cover object-center"
      />
    </div>

    <!-- 右侧：文字内容 -->
    <div class="flex flex-1 flex-col gap-3">
      <h2
        class="w-full text-left text-lg sm:text-2xl md:text-4xl font-medium tracking-tighter text-pretty bg-clip-text text-transparent bg-gradient-to-br from-primary via-foreground to-foreground"
      >
        Why I Started AAC For All
      </h2>
      <p
        class="w-full max-w-md text-left text-sm sm:text-normal md:text-lg font-normal text-balance"
      >
        I'm a parent of two autistic children—both non-speaking. I started this project from a simple wish: <strong>communication shouldn’t be limited by price tags or closed systems.</strong>
        <br /><br />
        AAC can be expensive and complicated—but it doesn’t have to be. All children and families deserve real, accessible choices.
        <br /><br />
        We are social beings. The need to be understood and affirmed is deeply human. But our minds can’t read each other—communication becomes the bridge between hearts.
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mt-4">
        <a
          href="mailto:helloluna520@gmail.com"
          class="relative inline-flex justify-center items-center px-4 py-2 sm:px-6 sm:py-3 sm:text-lg font-medium text-background bg-primary rounded-full perfect-shadow hover:bg-primary/90 transition-colors"
        >
          Contact me for AAC support
          <div
            class="absolute inset-0 m-[2px] rounded-full bg-gradient-to-b from-secondary via-primary to-primary -z-10 border-t-2 border-secondary"
          ></div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
